sector-profile-frontier = Frontier sector
sector-profile-asteroids = Asteroid cloud
sector-profile-wreckage = Wreckage field
sector-profile-radiation = Radiation fields
sector-profile-quiet = Quiet reach
space-environment-kind-dust = Dust cloud
space-environment-kind-asteroids = Asteroid stream
space-environment-kind-debris = Debris field
space-environment-kind-plasma = Plasma interference
space-environment-kind-radiation = Radiation field
space-environment-charted = [surveyed]
space-environment-ftl-blocked = Plasma interference prevents FTL preparation. Leave the marked boundary.
space-environment-sector = Sector: { $sector }. Profile: { $profile }. Regions surveyed: { $surveyed }/{ $total }.
space-environment-survey = Scan space environment
space-environment-survey-hint = Scan the environment through the context menu. Stay below 12 m/s in dust and 4 m/s to record a survey. Radiation requires protection; dense plasma disrupts radio and FTL.
space-environment-survey-cooldown = Instruments are processing the previous reading. Scans have a 20 second cooldown.
space-environment-survey-empty = No unsurveyed signals within 1800 m.
space-environment-survey-signal = Detected: { $kind }. Centre: ({ $x }, { $y }), distance { $distance } m. Approach the inner area to record a survey. Choose safe speed and protection.
space-environment-survey-slow = Slow down to 4 m/s for a stable reading.
space-environment-survey-complete = Survey complete: { $kind }. Data recorded in the journal.
space-environment-survey-recorded = This region is already recorded in the journal.
space-environment-survey-research = Awarded { $points } research points to the RnD server.
space-environment-survey-research-disk = Issued a disk containing { $points } RnD points. Upload it to a research server. If your hands are full, the disk is beside the console.
space-environment-survey-disk-name = Sector survey disk ({ $points } RnD)
ent-DeepLagoonSpaceSurveyDisk = sector survey data disk
    .desc = Research data from a previously uncharted space region. Insert into an RnD server to upload the points.

space-environment-route = Direct course: dust ~{ $dust } m; radiation ~{ $radiation } m (intensity weighted).
space-environment-route-ftl-blocked = FTL: plasma interference at departure or arrival.
space-environment-route-ftl-clear = FTL: no environmental endpoint interference detected. Other travel restrictions still apply.

space-environment-space-junk = space junk
space-environment-blue-wreck = drifting wreckage
space-environment-chromite = chromite asteroid
space-navigation-site-distress = Emergency supply capsule
space-navigation-site-dustsample = Charged dust sampler
space-navigation-site-archive = Sealed wreck archive
space-navigation-site-radiationcache = Research container in a shielded pocket
space-navigation-site-capacitor = Plasma accumulator
space-navigation-site-satellite = Broken orbital satellite
space-navigation-scan = Scan navigation signals
space-navigation-data = Recover signal data
space-navigation-cargo = Recover signal supplies
space-navigation-hint = Use the context menu to scan navigation signals. Within 80 m choose data or supplies: each find is consumed once. Data requires at most 2 m/s, supplies at most 4 m/s.
space-navigation-relay-hint = Bring a shuttle within 80 m. Its console can recover data or supplies using a remote probe.
space-navigation-signal = { $name }: ({ $x }, { $y }), { $distance } m. Environmental intensity: { $risk }%. Telemetry quality: { $quality }%.
space-navigation-clue-distress = An old automated SOS, no life signs. Choose a medkit or black-box research data. Beacons are rare.
space-navigation-clue-dustsample = The sampler lies in a thin corridor with 85% less dust load. Data grants research; extracting quartz discharges into the console (5 shock damage before protection).
space-navigation-clue-archive = Restore research data or dismantle the cargo section for metal. These choices are mutually exclusive.
space-navigation-clue-radiationcache = Radiation near the signal is reduced by 80%, not eliminated. Choose research data or an artifact fragment. Protection is needed on approach.
space-navigation-clue-capacitor = Available during a 20-second quiet window every 90 seconds. Choose research data or a charged cell. Radio interference weakens during the window; FTL restrictions remain. Ore-bearing chromite asteroids drift through the stream.
space-navigation-clue-satellite = Repairing telemetry for research requires 5 LV cable units held in hand. Alternatively dismantle the hull for metal.
space-navigation-window = Quiet window in: { $seconds } s (0 means open).
space-navigation-corridor = Thin corridor axis: ({ $ax }, { $ay }) to ({ $bx }, { $by }).
space-navigation-empty = No available unprocessed navigation signals within 1800 m.
space-navigation-approach = Bring the shuttle console within 80 m of an available signal. Scan to find its coordinates.
space-navigation-slow = Slow down: at most 2 m/s for data, 4 m/s for supplies.
space-navigation-wait = A plasma pulse blocks the probe. Scan and wait for the quiet window.
space-navigation-cable = Hold at least 5 units of LV cable to repair the satellite.
space-navigation-busy = The probe is returning. Retry in 20 seconds.
space-navigation-recorded = This find is already recorded in the journal.
space-navigation-delivered = Supplies delivered to the console and placed in a free hand when possible.
space-navigation-complete = Signal processed: { $name }. Result recorded in the journal.
ent-DeepLagoonNavigationRelay = abandoned navigation relay
    .desc = An old telemetry unit. A nearby shuttle console can recover its data or supplies.
